# The browser checks: `pnpm prd browser` (browser.sh) reads this for the suite's
# order, each check's cap and which checks never exit on their own.
# scripts/loops/check-areas maps changed files to these names; a unit test
# (checks.test.mjs) keeps the two in step.
#
# One check per line, in suite order:
#   check        the file's name without .mjs (scripts/browser-checks/<check>.mjs)
#   usual        its usual seconds for a full run on a quiet machine (from the logs)
#   cap          browser.sh kills it after this many seconds, as TIMEOUT (about 3×
#                usual, at least 120; --timeout overrides it). Unlisted checks: 600.
#   never-exits  yes: it never exits on its own, and is stopped 2 s after its
#                last line ("N/M passed", or signout-wipe's "errors:")
#   e2e          yes: in the lean end-to-end set, the suite (--suite, and
#                --changed's @suite): flows that need the server, sync or a real
#                build (sign-in and session, first sync, sign-out wipe, devices
#                converging, offline then reconnect, invites and email, the CSP
#                and the check build). no: still runnable, by name or through
#                --changed, but out of the suite until its screens move to
#                component tests (one backlog item per check).
#
# check            usual  cap  never-exits  e2e
